<h1 align="center">NetScope</h1>

<p align="center">
A lightweight, portable IP monitoring and geolocation dashboard for Windows 10 and 11, built in native C++17 and the Win32 API.
</p>

Overview

NetScope gives you instant, real-time visibility into your network identity without the overhead of heavy frameworks, runtimes, or background services. It monitors your public IP address, identifies your active local network interface, resolves your geographic location (country, state/region, city, and ISP), and discreetly sits in your Windows System Tray to alert you only when your IP changes.

Key Features

Public & Local IP Detection: Queries your current public IPv4 address and active local adapter with one-click manual refresh.

Accurate Geolocation: Displays your public IP's geographic location (e.g., USA, Virginia) alongside city and ISP details.

Smart Background Monitoring: Polls your public IP every 5 minutes in the background and notifies you only when a change occurs.

System Tray Integration: Closing the window minimizes NetScope to the system tray so monitoring continues uninterrupted until you explicitly choose to exit.

Zero Framework Bloat: Pure Win32 and C++17. No Electron, WebView2, .NET, Node.js, or external runtimes required.

Ultra-Lightweight Footprint: Typically consumes under 10 MB of RAM and 0.0% idle CPU.

Privacy-First: No telemetry, no background analytics, no account registration, and no administrator rights needed.

Design Language

NetScope features a custom-rendered, double-buffered dark dashboard inspired by modern mobile aesthetics:

Deep Dark Canvas: Surface background (#0B0B0F) with rounded cards (#24242A) and subtle borders.

High-Contrast Readability: Crisp white metrics paired with muted gray secondary indicators.

Per-Monitor DPI Awareness: Sharp scaling across standard and 4K displays.

Pixel-Art Cat Mascot: Custom brand identity with an embedded high-resolution application icon.

Download & Installation

Download the latest standalone executable from the [suspicious link removed] page:

Download NetScope.exe.

Move it to any folder of your choice.

Double-click to launch. No installer or prerequisites required.

Building from Source

NetScope is designed to compile cleanly on Windows 10 and 11 using either Microsoft Visual C++ (MSVC) or MinGW-w64.

Prerequisites

MSVC: Visual Studio 2019/2022 with the "Desktop development with C++" workload, or

MinGW / GCC: w64devkit or MSYS2 (GCC 10+).

Option 1: Build with MinGW / w64devkit

Open your terminal in the project directory and run:

cmd.exe /c build_mingw.bat


Option 2: Build with MSVC

Open the x64 Native Tools Command Prompt for VS and run:

build_msvc.bat


The portable binary will be created in build\NetScope.exe.

Privacy Policy

NetScope is built around user privacy:

Network requests are strictly outbound over HTTPS (TLS 1.2/1.3) solely to determine IP and geolocation metadata.

No user identifiers, device logs, or analytics are stored or transmitted.

For complete details, see our Privacy Policy.

Platform Support

Windows 10 (64-bit)

Windows 11 (64-bit)

Disclaimer

NetScope is intended for personal network diagnostic, administration, and monitoring purposes. Use NetScope responsibly and only with networks and systems you are authorized to inspect.
